<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guntram</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 532–592</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Saint Guntram, Gontran</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guntram was a Merovingian king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> who ruled the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> from 561 to 592. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a>, he received Burgundy with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> when the kingdom was divided among the brothers, and he ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalon-sur-saone">Chalon-sur-Saône</a>. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bretons">Bretons</a> and his brothers' kingdoms and was later venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guntram.jpg" alt="Guntram" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Atelier de Chalon-sur-Saône · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tiers_de_sou_de_Gontran_frapp%C3%A9_%C3%A0_Chalon-sur-Sa%C3%B4ne.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
